1
00:07:08,571 --> 00:07:14,571
When men ruled as gods, one was chosen to change the world.

2
00:14:17,142 --> 00:14:23,142
Exodus: Gods and Kings is a adventure, drama,
action film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:21:25,714 --> 00:21:31,714
The defiant leader Moses rises up against the Egyptian Pharaoh Ramses, setting 400,000 slaves on a
monumental journey of escape from Egypt and its terrifying cycle of deadly plagues.

4
00:28:34,285 --> 00:28:40,285
Moses, played by Christian Bale.

5
00:35:42,857 --> 00:35:48,857
Ramses II, played by Joel Edgerton.

6
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Nun, played by Ben Kingsley.

7
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Sethos I, played by John Turturro.

8
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
Joshua, played by Aaron Paul.

9
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Nefertari, played by Golshifteh Farahani.

10
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Exodus: Gods and Kings is a 2014 biblical epic film directed and produced by Ridley Scott,
and written by Adam Cooper, Bill Collage, Jeffrey Caine, and Steven Zaillian.

11
01:18:34,285 --> 01:18:40,285
The film stars Christian Bale, Joel Edgerton, John Turturro, Aaron
Paul, Ben Mendelsohn, Sigourney Weaver, and Ben Kingsley.

12
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It is inspired by the biblical episode of the Exodus of the Hebrews from
Egypt led by Moses and related in the Book of Exodus.

13
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
Development on the film was first announced by Scott in June 2012.

14
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Filming occurred primarily in Spain beginning in October 2013, with
additional filming at Pinewood Studios in England.

15
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
The film was released on December 12, 2014, by
20th Century Fox, to mixed reviews.

16
01:54:17,142 --> 01:54:23,142
Critics praised the visual effects and cast performances, but criticized its pacing,
screenplay, lack of emotional heft, and inaccuracy to the source material.

17
02:01:25,714 --> 02:01:31,714
The film also received accusations of whitewashing for its primarily Caucasian cast, and was
banned in Egypt and in the United Arab Emirates for "historical inaccuracies".

18
02:08:34,285 --> 02:08:40,285
It was considered a financial disappointment, earning $268
million worldwide on a budget of $140–200 million.

19
02:15:42,857 --> 02:15:48,857
The film explores themes of moses, bible, racism, slave, ancient egypt.

20
02:22:51,428 --> 02:22:57,428
The tone is emotional.
